\title{Computing GCD via the Euclidean algorithm}
\date{2026-04-16T22:42:06Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{[Computing the GCD via factoring](00F0) is not very practical for larger numbers, because factoring takes a long time. It turns out there is a much better way that is actually used in practice. To see why it works, we’ll first need a few lemmas and theorems about #{\gcd}.}

\transclude{00GQ}   % GCD arguments can be subtracted
\transclude{00F3}   % GCD is commutative

